# The keys that may sign a GroundWork seal, in git's SSH allowed-signers format:
#
#   <principal> namespaces="git" <keytype> <public key>
#
# One line per key. Nothing is listed yet, and that is the honest state of this
# environment: the agents run inside the container, and any key the container
# can use, they can read. A key here that they could reach would be a control
# in name only.
#
# So the tool never holds or creates a signing key. It only verifies, against
# this file. Every seal it grants is unsigned, and every line it prints about
# one says so.
#
# When the owner's key is added here, unsigned stops being loud and starts being
# blocking, and that flip is a major battery bump. R4 names the deferral.
